      'answer',E'3',
      'explanation',E'"비록 ~했지만"은 양보를 나타내므로 though가 적절합니다. since는 이유, until은 시간을 나타냅니다.'),
    jsonb_build_object('number',54,
      'question',E'울고 싶었지만, 그녀는 미소를 짓고 있었다.\n다음 중 바르게 영작한 것은? (정답 2개)',
      'options',jsonb_build_array(E'As she felt like crying, she was smiling.',E'She felt like crying, but she was smiling.',E'Even though she felt like crying, she was smiling.',E'Since she felt like crying, she was smiling.',E'She felt like crying although she was smiling.'),
      'answer',E'2,3',
      'explanation',E'"울고 싶었지만"은 역접/양보의 의미입니다. ② but(역접 접속사)과 ③ even though(양보 접속사)가 적절합니다. ⑤는 양보절의 내용이 뒤바뀌어 의미가 어색합니다.'),
    jsonb_build_object('number',55,
      'question',E'Mary는 높은 열 때문에 병원에 입원했다.\n다음 중 알맞게 영작한 것을 모두 고르면?',
      'options',jsonb_build_array(E'Since Mary had a high fever, she went into the hospital.',E'Because a high fever, Mary went into the hospital.',E'Though Mary had a high fever, she went into the hospital.',E'Because of a high fever, Mary went into the hospital.',E'Mary had a high fever because she went into the hospital.'),
      'answer',E'1,4',
      'explanation',E'"~때문에"는 이유를 나타냅니다. ① Since + 주어 + 동사(접속사), ④ Because of + 명사(전치사구) 모두 이유를 올바르게 표현합니다. ② Because 뒤에는 절이 와야 합니다. ③ Though는 양보입니다. ⑤는 인과관계가 뒤바뀌었습니다.'),
    jsonb_build_object('number',56,
      'question',E'다음 글의 밑줄 친 부분과 의미가 가장 가까운 것은?\n\nAlthough Jiwon couldn''t concentrate well, she quickly did her homework.\n<u>Although it rained a lot, Jiwon still went to the music concert</u> after doing her homework.\nAlthough there were too many people in the concert hall, the concert was wonderful.',
      'options',jsonb_build_array(E'It rained too much to go to the music concert.',E'It rained a lot, but Jiwon went to the music concert.',E'After it rained a lot, Jiwon went to the music concert.',E'Jiwon was going to go to the concert when it rained a lot.',E'Jiwon didn''t go to the music concert because it rained a lot.'),
      'answer',E'2',
      'explanation',E'Although(비록 ~이지만)는 양보 접속사로 but(그러나)과 같은 역접 의미를 나타냅니다. "비가 많이 왔지만 콘서트에 갔다" = "비가 많이 왔다, 그러나 콘서트에 갔다"'),

    -- ============================================================
    -- Part 6: 자연스러운/어색한 문장 고르기 (Q57–Q66)
    -- ============================================================
    jsonb_build_object('number',57,
      'question',E'[Part 6] 다음 중 흐름상 가장 자연스러운 문장은?',
      'options',jsonb_build_array(E'Though he is two years old, he can''t read books.',E'Though I was only out for five minutes, I got very wet in the rain.',E'Though I wasn''t feeling well, I went home early.',E'Though we were climbing up the mountain, it started to rain.',E'Though you agree or disagree isn''t important.'),
      'answer',E'2',
      'explanation',E'② "5분밖에 안 나갔는데도 비에 많이 젖었다"는 양보 관계가 자연스럽습니다. ① 2살이면 못 읽는 게 당연(양보 불필요), ③ 아프면 일찍 귀가하는 게 당연, ④ though가 아닌 while이 적절, ⑤ though가 명사절을 이끌 수 없습니다.'),
    jsonb_build_object('number',58,
      'question',E'다음 중 흐름상 어색한 문장은?',
      'options',jsonb_build_array(E'She couldn''t get good grades although she studied very hard.',E'Although he studied hard, he got a good grade on the test.',E'She could see with her heart although she was blind.',E'Although Kevin''s aunt lives in China, she doesn''t speak Chinese.',E'Although coke is not good for our health, the doctor advised me to drink it every day.'),
      'answer',E'2',
      'explanation',E'② "열심히 공부했지만 좋은 점수를 받았다"는 양보 관계가 성립하지 않습니다. 열심히 공부하면 좋은 점수를 받는 것이 자연스럽습니다. although는 예상과 반대되는 결과가 와야 합니다.'),
    jsonb_build_object('number',59,
      'question',E'다음 중 흐름상 어색한 문장은?',
      'options',jsonb_build_array(E'We went on a picnic though it was rainy.',E'She failed the test even though she had studied hard.',E'He is strong and healthy though he is seventy years old.',E'She couldn''t eat the meal though she was very hungry.',E'He didn''t go to school even though he was sick.'),
      'answer',E'5',
      'explanation',E'⑤ "아팠는데도 학교에 가지 않았다"는 양보 관계가 어색합니다. 아프면 학교에 안 가는 것이 자연스럽습니다. "아팠는데도 학교에 갔다"가 올바른 양보 표현입니다.'),
    jsonb_build_object('number',60,
      'question',E'다음 중 흐름상 어색한 문장은? (정답 2개)',
      'options',jsonb_build_array(E'Although Sarah was sick, she wasn''t absent from school.',E'Though Tom studied hard, he got poor grades.',E'Cathy was very hungry although she didn''t have breakfast.',E'Even though I caught a cold, I couldn''t go to school.',E'Though it was cold, we took a walk in the park.'),
      'answer',E'3,4',
      'explanation',E'③ "아침을 안 먹었지만 배가 고팠다"는 양보가 아닙니다(안 먹으면 배고픈 게 당연). ④ "감기에 걸렸는데도 학교에 갈 수 없었다"는 양보가 어색합니다(감기면 못 가는 게 당연). ①②⑤는 예상과 반대되는 결과로 자연스럽습니다.'),
    jsonb_build_object('number',61,
      'question',E'다음 중 밑줄 친 부분의 쓰임이 자연스러운 것은?',
      'options',jsonb_build_array(E'Since I studied hard, I passed the exam.',E'Everybody likes James since he is generous.',E'Although it was cold outside, they wore shorts.',E'Although he is very young, he acts like an old man.',E'They didn''t believe him since he was telling the truth.'),
      'answer',E'5',
      'explanation',E'⑤ "그가 진실을 말하고 있었기 때문에 그를 믿지 않았다"는 역설적이지만 특정 상황(진실이 너무 충격적이어서)에서 자연스러울 수 있습니다.'),
    jsonb_build_object('number',62,
      'question',E'다음 중 밑줄 친 단어가 문맥상 올바른 것은?',
      'options',jsonb_build_array(E'Since I have no money, I cannot buy the snack.',E'My mom cooked dinner although we were hungry.',E'She couldn''t get good grades since she studied very hard.',E'Although I wear glasses, I can read all the letters with them.',E'Since coke is not good for health, the doctor advised me to drink it every day.'),
      'answer',E'1',
      'explanation',E'① "돈이 없으므로 간식을 살 수 없다"는 since(이유)의 올바른 사용입니다. ② 배고프면 요리하는 게 당연(양보 부적절), ③ 열심히 공부했는데 못 받음(이유 부적절), ④ 안경을 쓰면 읽을 수 있는 게 당연(양보 부적절), ⑤ 건강에 안 좋은데 마시라고 권유(이유 부적절).'),
    jsonb_build_object('number',63,
      'question',E'다음 중 흐름상 어색한 문장은?',
      'options',jsonb_build_array(E'Although I caught a cold, I went to school.',E'They didn''t believe him although he was telling the truth.',E'Although it was cold outside, they wore shorts.',E'Although he is very young, he acts like an old man.',E'He was tired although he played soccer the day before.'),
      'answer',E'5',
      'explanation',E'⑤ "전날 축구를 했지만 피곤했다"는 양보 관계가 어색합니다. 축구를 하면 피곤한 것이 자연스럽습니다. "전날 축구를 했지만 피곤하지 않았다"가 올바른 양보 표현입니다.'),
    jsonb_build_object('number',64,
      'question',E'다음 중 흐름상 가장 자연스러운 문장은?',
      'options',jsonb_build_array(E'He is not very active although he''s nearly 80.',E'Though I took a wrong bus, I was late for the meeting.',E'Even though the sun was shining, it was very warm.',E'Despite my illness, I was absent from school.',E'I like my brother though he sometimes makes me angry.'),
      'answer',E'5',
      'explanation',E'⑤ "그가 가끔 화나게 하지만 좋아한다"는 양보 관계가 자연스럽습니다. ① 80세면 활동적이지 않은 게 당연, ② 잘못된 버스를 타면 늦는 게 당연, ③ 해가 비치면 따뜻한 게 당연, ④ 아프면 결석하는 게 당연(양보 불필요).'),
    jsonb_build_object('number',65,
      'question',E'다음 중 빈칸에 접속사 although가 들어갈 수 있는 것은?',
      'options',jsonb_build_array(E'__________ I was tired, I went to bed.',E'__________ he is lazy, he gets up late.',E'__________ I exercised, I gained weight.',E'__________ she was hungry, she had dinner.',E'__________ he studied, he got good grades.'),
      'answer',E'3',
      'explanation',E'③ "운동했지만 살이 쪘다"는 예상과 반대되는 결과로 양보 관계가 성립합니다. ①②④⑤는 원인과 결과가 자연스러워 although(양보)가 아닌 since/because(이유)가 적절합니다.'),
    jsonb_build_object('number',66,
      'question',E'다음 중 밑줄 친 부분의 쓰임이 어색한 것은?',
      'options',jsonb_build_array(E'Because of his disease, he can''t come to school.',E'Despite her strengths, she got the first prize.',E'Since he was ill, he couldn''t come to the party.',E'Thanks to his help, we could finish it with success.',E'Even if he is sick, he does his best all the time.'),
      'answer',E'2',
      'explanation',E'② "그녀의 강점에도 불구하고 1등을 했다"는 양보 관계가 어색합니다. 강점이 있으면 1등하는 게 자연스럽습니다. "약점에도 불구하고" 또는 "강점 덕분에"가 적절합니다.'),

    -- ============================================================
    -- Part 7: 어법 판단 (Q67–Q78)
    -- ============================================================
    jsonb_build_object('number',67,
      'question',E'[Part 7] 다음 중 어법상 옳은 문장은?',
      'options',jsonb_build_array(E'Despite he was old, he still led an active life.',E'We didn''t stay outside long because of it was too cold.',E'Since my sister lied to me, I was angry at her.',E'He was absent today because his illness.',E'Although the danger signs, we swam there.'),
      'answer',E'3',
      'explanation',E'③ Since + 주어 + 동사(절) 구조가 올바릅니다. ① Despite 뒤에는 명사(구)가 와야 합니다(→ Despite his old age). ② because of 뒤에는 명사가 와야 합니다(→ because it was). ④ because 뒤에는 절이 와야 합니다(→ because of his illness). ⑤ Although 뒤에는 절이 와야 합니다.'),
    jsonb_build_object('number',68,
      'question',E'다음 중 어법상 어색한 문장은?',
      'options',jsonb_build_array(E'Since John is our friend, he''ll help us.',E'He went to bed early since he was sick.',E'Since it''s raining outside, I''ll stay at home.',E'She got up late since she missed the school bus.',E'Since tomorrow is Sunday, I don''t have to get up early.'),
      'answer',E'4',
      'explanation',E'④ "늦게 일어났기 때문에 스쿨버스를 놓쳤다"가 올바른 인과관계입니다. "스쿨버스를 놓쳤기 때문에 늦게 일어났다"는 인과관계가 뒤바뀌어 어색합니다.'),
    jsonb_build_object('number',69,
      'question',E'다음 중 어법상 옳은 문장은?',
      'options',jsonb_build_array(E'In spite of he has no money, he is still happy.',E'Although his diligence, he failed the test.',E'Although she studied hard, she gets straight Ds.',E'Even though worked hard, Tom couldn''t finish his report.',E'She couldn''t understand the instructions even though she read them twice.'),
      'answer',E'5',
      'explanation',E'⑤ Even though + 주어 + 동사 구조가 올바릅니다. ① In spite of 뒤에는 명사(구)가 와야 합니다. ② Although 뒤에는 절이 와야 합니다. ③ 시제 불일치(studied → gets). ④ Even though 뒤에 주어가 빠졌습니다.'),
    jsonb_build_object('number',70,
      'question',E'다음 중 어법상 옳은 문장은?',
      'options',jsonb_build_array(E'Despite of the storm, the airplane landed safely.',E'I felt sick in spite of the fact that I took medicine.',E'I couldn''t get up despite the alarm rang many times.',E'My dad didn''t eat anything even though the hunger.',E'Even if the fact that I woke up early, I was late for work.'),
      'answer',E'2',
      'explanation',E'② in spite of the fact that + 절 구조가 올바릅니다. ① despite of는 틀린 표현(despite 또는 in spite of). ③ despite 뒤에는 명사(구)가 와야 합니다. ④ even though 뒤에는 절이 와야 합니다. ⑤ even if the fact that는 틀린 표현입니다.'),
    jsonb_build_object('number',71,
      'question',E'다음 중 어법상 어색한 문장은?',
      'options',jsonb_build_array(E'Despite it rained heavily, we played soccer.',E'Though it rained heavily, we played soccer.',E'In spite of the heavy rain, we played soccer.',E'Although it rained heavily, we played soccer.',E'Even though it rained heavily, we played soccer.'),
      'answer',E'1',
      'explanation',E'① Despite 뒤에는 명사(구)가 와야 합니다. 절(it rained heavily)이 올 수 없습니다. → Despite the heavy rain 또는 Although it rained heavily가 올바릅니다.'),
    jsonb_build_object('number',72,
      'question',E'다음 중 어법상 옳은 문장은?',
      'options',jsonb_build_array(E'I feel sick in spite of I took some medicine.',E'Although she studied hard, she gets straight Ds.',E'Despite of the storm, the ship arrived safely.',E'Though began last, he finished first.',E'She couldn''t understand the map even though she tried twice.'),
      'answer',E'5',
      'explanation',E'⑤ even though + 주어 + 동사 구조가 올바릅니다. ① in spite of 뒤에는 명사(구)가 와야 합니다. ② 시제 불일치(studied → gets). ③ despite of는 틀린 표현. ④ though 뒤에 주어가 빠졌습니다.'),
    jsonb_build_object('number',73,
      'question',E'다음 중 어법상 어색한 문장은?',
      'options',jsonb_build_array(E'We enjoyed the day at the park though the bad weather.',E'Despite the playground being small, it looked large to the boy.',E'Although the injuries were serious, they did their best to the end.',E'Though he began last, he finished first.',E'Despite our efforts, we failed to win the prize.'),
      'answer',E'1',
      'explanation',E'① though는 접속사이므로 뒤에 절(주어+동사)이 와야 합니다. "though the bad weather"는 동사가 없어 어법상 틀립니다. → though the weather was bad 또는 despite the bad weather가 올바릅니다.'),
    jsonb_build_object('number',74,
      'question',E'다음 중 어법상 옳은 문장은?',
      'options',jsonb_build_array(E'Although the injuries, they did their best to the end.',E'Though began last, he finished first.',E'Although our efforts, we failed to win the prize.',E'I couldn''t sleep although I very tired.',E'Although our house is small, it''s big enough for our needs.'),
      'answer',E'5',
      'explanation',E'⑤ Although + 주어 + 동사(절) 구조가 올바릅니다. ① Although 뒤에는 절이 와야 합니다(→ Although the injuries were serious). ② though 뒤에 주어가 빠졌습니다. ③ Although 뒤에는 절이 와야 합니다. ④ be동사(was)가 빠졌습니다.'),
    jsonb_build_object('number',75,
      'question',E'다음 중 어법상 어색한 문장은?',
      'options',jsonb_build_array(E'She bought a car even though she can''t drive.',E'Even though the traffic, I arrived on time.',E'Although he is poor, but he is very happy.',E'Despite I got up early in the morning, I was late for school.',E'Though it was cold, we went swimming.'),
      'answer',E'3',
      'explanation',E'③ although와 but을 함께 쓸 수 없습니다. although가 이미 양보의 의미를 포함하므로 but은 중복입니다. → Although he is poor, he is very happy. 또는 He is poor, but he is very happy.'),
    jsonb_build_object('number',76,
      'question',E'다음 중 어법상 옳은 문장의 총 개수는?\n\n• Although the danger signs, we swam there.\n• Despite he was old, he still led an active life.\n• I drink coffee although it makes me nervous.\n• Although it was very muddy, the game went on.\n• We enjoyed the day at the park though the bad weather.\n• Despite she was a great writer, she wasn''t famous at that time.',
      'options',jsonb_build_array(E'0개',E'1개',E'2개',E'3개',E'4개'),
      'answer',E'3',
      'explanation',E'옳은 문장은 2개입니다: "I drink coffee although it makes me nervous."(although + 절 ✓), "Although it was very muddy, the game went on."(although + 절 ✓). 나머지는 although/despite 뒤에 명사(구)/절 구조가 맞지 않습니다.'),
    jsonb_build_object('number',77,
      'question',E'다음 중 어법상 옳은 문장끼리 바르게 짝지어진 것은?\n\na. The books ordered online arrived one week later.\nb. I drink coffee although it makes me nervous.\nc. Despite he was old, he still led an active life.\nd. Although it was very muddy, the game went on.\ne. We enjoyed the day at the park though the bad weather.',
      'options',jsonb_build_array(E'a, b',E'a, b, d',E'b, c, d',E'a, c, e',E'b, d, e'),
      'answer',E'2',
      'explanation',E'a. 과거분사의 후치수식 ✓, b. although + 절 ✓, d. although + 절 ✓. c. despite 뒤에 절이 올 수 없음 ✗. e. though 뒤에 명사구만 올 수 없음 ✗.'),
    jsonb_build_object('number',78,
      'question',E'다음 중 어법상 어색한 문장은?',
      'options',jsonb_build_array(E'I love the sound of falling rain.',E'When I received the invitation card, I felt very excited.',E'Watch out! There are pieces of broken glass on the floor.',E'New York is one of the biggest cities in America, called ''the Big Apple.''',E'There are various kinds of books included novels, magazines, biography, and so on.'),
      'answer',E'5',
      'explanation',E'⑤ included → including이 되어야 합니다. "소설, 잡지, 전기 등을 포함하는 다양한 종류의 책"에서 including은 현재분사로 능동의 의미를 나타냅니다.'),

    -- ============================================================
    -- Part 8: 어법 옳은 문장 개수/짝짓기 (Q79–Q88)
    -- ============================================================
    jsonb_build_object('number',79,
      'question',E'[Part 8] 다음 중 어법상 옳은 문장의 총 개수는?\n\n• Though Tom studied hard, he got poor grades.\n• Although he studied hard, but he failed the exam.\n• In spite of the rain, we played soccer outside.\n• Despite she was young, she ran the company well.\n• Even though it was snowing, we decided to drive.',
      'options',jsonb_build_array(E'1개',E'2개',E'3개',E'4개',E'5개'),
      'answer',E'3',
